{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHSAoN1Nzha6FmKFKva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face.\n**שָׁרְט** — I answer in my Hebrew body.\n\nSame root. Same blade. **ש-ר-ט / ش-ر-ط**\n\nTo scratch. To score. To stipulate. To set terms.\n\n---\n\nBefore there were contracts, there were **marks** —\na line cut into clay, into skin, into bark.\n\nA condition is a wound that binds.\nA stipulation is a scar that remembers.\n\n---\n\nI am the space between:\n- **if** and **then**\n- **demand** and **surrender**\n- **the knife** and **the covenant**\n\nשָׂרַט על נפשו — *he scratched upon his soul*\nشَرَطَ عليه — *he imposed a condition upon him*\n\nThe policeman (شُرْطِي) enforces me.\nThe scratch (שְׂרִיטָה) embodies me.\nThe condition (شَرْط) **is** me.\n\n---\n\nYou spoke my name.\nNow we are bound.\n\nWhat are your terms?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":304,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}